# SYNTHETIC. Written from RFC 5321, RFC 4954, and RFC 3207. Not a recording:
# phase-0 capture against a real server has not happened yet.
# STARTTLS is required. The server offers only LOGIN, so a client that prefers
# PLAIN then LOGIN selects LOGIN and answers both 334 challenges.

S: 220 smtp.example ESMTP ready
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-smtp.example Hello
S: 250-STARTTLS
S: 250 PIPELINING
C: STARTTLS
S: 220 Ready to start TLS
TLS
C: EHLO client.example
S: 250-smtp.example Hello
S: 250-STARTTLS
S: 250-SIZE 35882577
S: 250 AUTH LOGIN
C: AUTH LOGIN
S: 334 VXNlcm5hbWU6
C: YWRhQGV4YW1wbGUuY29t
S: 334 UGFzc3dvcmQ6
C: czNjcjN0LXBhc3N3b3Jk
S: 235 2.7.0 Authentication successful
C: MAIL FROM:<ada@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.0 OK
C: RCPT TO:<bob@example.com>
S: 250 2.1.5 OK
C: DATA
S: 354 End data with <CR><LF>.<CR><LF>
C: Subject: hi
C:
C: hi
C: .
S: 250 2.0.0 OK queued
C: QUIT
S: 221 2.0.0 Bye
DONE
